<Layout title="About — Jayden Park" description="Meet Jayden Park: fine artist, visual designer, and Vanderbilt student exploring art, business, and human connection."><div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">A little beyond the work</p><h1>Hi, I’m Jayden.<br/><em>Curiosity comes first.</em></h1></header><div class="about-layout"><div class="about-text"><p>I’m a fine artist and visual designer, originally based in Vancouver and studying Human and Organizational Development, Business, and Art at Vanderbilt University.</p><p>My work moves between traditional art, digital interfaces, and graphics made for communities. This portfolio brings those different parts of my creative practice together.</p><p>I’ve always liked giving an idea something tangible to live on—a piece of paper, a screen, or a visual that someone stops to look at.</p><h2>From a pencil<br/><em>to possibilities.</em></h2><p>My artist’s statement starts with childhood scribbles and a faithful Faber-Castell HB pencil. Drawing has long been a way to follow an idea before knowing exactly where it will go.</p><a class="text-link" href="/writing/10-tips-for-creating-engaging-interactive-art/">Read my artist’s statement ↗</a></div><figure class="about-art"><Picture image={dream.images[0]} alt="DREAM, an artwork by Jayden Park" eager/><figcaption>A glimpse into my imagination.<br/>DREAM — from the fine-art collection.</figcaption></figure></div><section class="personal-grid" aria-label="A few personal favorites"><div><h3>Places in my story</h3><p>Seoul<br/>Vancouver<br/>Nashville</p></div><div><h3>Things I gravitate to</h3><p>Golfing & karaoke<br/>Café hunting<br/>A good bubble tea</p></div><div><h3>A few favorites</h3><p>Tonkatsu<br/>Bibimbap<br/>Making something new</p></div></section><section class="about-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">Where creativity meets people</p><h2>Art, with<br/><em>another perspective.</em></h2></div><div class="about-text"><p>My experience includes creative and marketing roles with KUSA, VAPS, Youth in Policy, and Lambda Phi Epsilon. These communities give my visual work a place to connect with people.</p><a class="text-link" href="/playground/">Explore the graphics ↗</a><div class="recognition"><p class="eyebrow">Fine-art recognition</p><p>The Vanderbilt Review<br/>The Scholastic Art & Writing Awards</p></div><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jaydenpark2005/">Professional background on LinkedIn ↗</a></div></section></div></Layout>
